WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
Aisha receives a premium payment while the agency is short on

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:08.380
cash. That money is not a convenient loan for rent.

3
00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.760
A producer handles money belonging to others with fiduciary responsibilities.

4
00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:19.600
Misappropriating, converting or unlawfully withholding money can support

5
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.620
license discipline. Keep an accurate record of receipt, the client,

6
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.140
the insurer, the purpose and the amount.

7
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:32.640
The fact that a commission will eventually be earned does not

8
00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.820
make the entire premium the agency's income.

9
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.620
Follow the authorized payment and accounting process from the start.

10
00:00:41.586 --> 00:00:46.706
Maryland's premium-account regulation defines prompt remittance as sending

11
00:00:46.706 --> 00:00:50.906
premium money to the carrier or insured no later than the

12
00:00:50.906 --> 00:00:53.626
close of the fifth business day following receipt.

13
00:00:54.726 --> 00:00:58.326
A producer who does not make prompt remittance must maintain the

14
00:00:58.326 --> 00:01:02.686
premium in one or more premium accounts, separate from operating and

15
00:01:02.686 --> 00:01:07.026
personal accounts. Do not count business days as calendar days.

16
00:01:07.966 --> 00:01:11.966
A premium account is restricted money, not an everyday spending account.

17
00:01:12.726 --> 00:01:16.426
A documented process should show where the money is and who

18
00:01:16.426 --> 00:01:17.466
is entitled to it.

19
00:01:18.204 --> 00:01:20.524
Not every mixture of funds is the same.

20
00:01:21.284 --> 00:01:25.504
Maryland permits voluntary deposits into a premium account and generally

21
00:01:25.504 --> 00:01:30.384
allows multiple carriers' premiums there unless prohibited by a carrier or

22
00:01:30.384 --> 00:01:34.564
a special rule. It prohibits mixing the premium account with an

23
00:01:34.564 --> 00:01:36.304
operating or personal account.

24
00:01:37.124 --> 00:01:41.364
Withdrawals are limited to authorized purposes, such as paying carriers,

25
00:01:41.924 --> 00:01:46.400
transferring permitted commissions and making authorized returns.

26
00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:50.204
A withdrawal cannot leave less than the required aggregate net premiums,

27
00:01:50.664 --> 00:01:53.284
return premiums and unremitted deposits.

28
00:01:54.524 --> 00:01:58.844
Reconcile the account; do not guess the available balance from the

29
00:01:58.844 --> 00:02:03.622
bank total. Compensation for selling, soliciting or negotiating insurance

30
00:02:03.622 --> 00:02:08.242
generally goes to a licensed producer, subject to statutory exceptions.

31
00:02:10.242 --> 00:02:14.002
Paying through a different label does not cure unlicensed selling.

32
00:02:14.722 --> 00:02:18.602
Maryland also permits certain renewal or deferred commissions to a person

33
00:02:18.602 --> 00:02:22.762
who formerly held the required life producer license and appointment.

34
00:02:23.362 --> 00:02:27.042
Other permitted payments or assignments to people who do not sell,

35
00:02:27.722 --> 00:02:32.382
solicit or negotiate must still avoid unlawful rebating or inducements.

36
00:02:33.162 --> 00:02:37.322
Identify what the person actually did, their required authority when

37
00:02:37.322 --> 00:02:39.502
applicable, and the kind of compensation.

38
00:02:40.392 --> 00:02:44.372
A producer cannot simply add any charge the customer will tolerate.

39
00:02:45.092 --> 00:02:48.752
Maryland restricts collecting premiums or charges different from those

40
00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:52.052
applicable to the insurance, with specified exceptions.

41
00:02:53.072 --> 00:02:56.502
One exception permits a placement-service fee of no more than fifteen

42
00:02:56.502 --> 00:02:59.532
percent of the premium when the insurer does not pay commissions.

43
00:03:00.552 --> 00:03:04.072
For a one-thousand-dollar premium, that ceiling is one hundred fifty dollars.

44
00:03:05.152 --> 00:03:08.972
It is not permission to add fifteen percent to every commissioned

45
00:03:08.972 --> 00:03:13.992
policy. Verify the applicable exception, disclose accurately

46
00:03:14.672 --> 00:03:16.632
and keep a record of the authorized charge.

47
00:03:17.610 --> 00:03:21.870
Record retention depends on the document and rule.

48
00:03:22.790 --> 00:03:28.050
Maryland appointment records are kept while the appointment is active and

49
00:03:28.050 --> 00:03:29.750
at least five years afterward.

50
00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:35.250
Under the annuity recommendation rule, covered transaction records are

51
00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:39.690
maintained for seven years after the insurer completes the transaction.

52
00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:45.490
An insurer may keep those records for a producer, but the

53
00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:50.330
producer should verify that arrangement rather than assume it exists.

54
00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:55.310
Preserve readable, retrievable documents and signatures.

55
00:03:56.310 --> 00:04:01.490
Good records connect the advice, disclosure, payment and

56
00:04:01.490 --> 00:04:06.550
final transaction so another reviewer can understand what actually happened.
